---
---

<div class="px-5 w-full flex justify-center">
    <div class="w-full max-w-4xl text-left">
        <details class="border-b border-zinc-800 group" name="faq" id="faq-1">
            <summary
                class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-5 font-medium text-white hover:bg-zinc-700 gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none"
            >
                <span class="font-medium text-lg">
                    Where can I download the latest PacketEvents release?
                </span>
                <svg
                    class="w-3 h-3 rotate-180 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-0 transition-transform"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                    fill="none"
                    viewBox="0 0 10 6"
                >
                    <path
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        stroke-linecap="round"
                        stroke-linejoin="round"
                        stroke-width="2"
                        d="M9 5 5 1 1 5"
                    ></path>
                </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="p-5 text-zinc-200">
                <p>
                    You can download the latest release on{" "}
                    <a
                        href="https://modrinth.com/plugin/packetevents"
                        class="text-indigo-700">Modrinth</a
                    >.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="border-b border-zinc-800 group" name="faq" id="faq-2">
            <summary
                class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-5 font-medium text-white hover:bg-zinc-700 gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none"
            >
                <span class="font-medium text-lg">
                    Where can I find PacketEvents development builds?
                </span>
                <svg
                    class="w-3 h-3 rotate-180 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-0 transition-transform"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                    fill="none"
                    viewBox="0 0 10 6"
                >
                    <path
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        stroke-linecap="round"
                        stroke-linejoin="round"
                        stroke-width="2"
                        d="M9 5 5 1 1 5"
                    ></path>
                </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="p-5 text-zinc-200">
                <p>
                    You can download development builds on{" "}
                    <a
                        href="https://ci.codemc.io/job/retrooper/job/packetevents/"
                        class="text-indigo-700">Jenkins</a
                    >.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="border-b border-zinc-800 group" name="faq" id="faq-3">
            <summary
                class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-5 font-medium text-white hover:bg-zinc-700 gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none"
            >
                <span class="font-medium text-lg">
                    What Minecraft version does PacketEvents support?
                </span>
                <svg
                    class="w-3 h-3 rotate-180 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-0 transition-transform"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                    fill="none"
                    viewBox="0 0 10 6"
                >
                    <path
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        stroke-linecap="round"
                        stroke-linejoin="round"
                        stroke-width="2"
                        d="M9 5 5 1 1 5"
                    ></path>
                </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="p-5 text-zinc-200">
                <p>
                    PacketEvents supports Minecraft versions
                    <span class="text-indigo-700"> 1.8</span>-
                    <span class="text-indigo-700">latest </span>
                    Java Edition.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="border-b border-zinc-800 group" name="faq" id="faq-4">
            <summary
                class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-5 font-medium text-white hover:bg-zinc-700 gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none"
            >
                <span class="font-medium text-lg">
                    Where can I learn to use PacketEvents?
                </span>
                <svg
                    class="w-3 h-3 rotate-180 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-0 transition-transform"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                    fill="none"
                    viewBox="0 0 10 6"
                >
                    <path
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        stroke-linecap="round"
                        stroke-linejoin="round"
                        stroke-width="2"
                        d="M9 5 5 1 1 5"
                    ></path>
                </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="p-5 text-zinc-200">
                <p>Currently, the guide is still being worked on...</p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="border-b border-zinc-800 group" name="faq" id="faq-5">
            <summary
                class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-5 font-medium text-white hover:bg-zinc-700 gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none"
            >
                <span class="font-medium text-lg">
                    Is PacketEvents free software?
                </span>
                <svg
                    class="w-3 h-3 rotate-180 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-0 transition-transform"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                    fill="none"
                    viewBox="0 0 10 6"
                >
                    <path
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        stroke-linecap="round"
                        stroke-linejoin="round"
                        stroke-width="2"
                        d="M9 5 5 1 1 5"
                    ></path>
                </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="p-5 text-zinc-200">
                <p>
                    Yes, Packet Events is{" "}
                    <a
                        target="_"
                        href="https://www.gnu.org/philosophy/free-sw.en.html"
                        class="text-indigo-700">Free Software</a
                    >. It uses the{" "}
                    <a
                        target="_"
                        href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.en.html"
                        class="text-indigo-700">GPLv3</a
                    >{" "}
                    license.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="border-b border-zinc-800 group" name="faq" id="faq-6">
            <summary
                class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-5 font-medium text-white hover:bg-zinc-700 gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none"
            >
                <span class="font-medium text-lg">
                    Does PacketEvents have a Discord server?
                </span>
                <svg
                    class="w-3 h-3 rotate-180 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-0 transition-transform"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                    fill="none"
                    viewBox="0 0 10 6"
                >
                    <path
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        stroke-linecap="round"
                        stroke-linejoin="round"
                        stroke-width="2"
                        d="M9 5 5 1 1 5"
                    ></path>
                </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="p-5 text-zinc-200">
                <p>
                    Join the
                    <a
                        href="https://discord.gg/DVHxPPxHZc"
                        class="text-indigo-700"> PacketEvents Discord Server </a
                    >
                    and receive community support!
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="border-b border-zinc-800 group" name="faq" id="faq-7">
            <summary
                class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-5 font-medium text-white hover:bg-zinc-700 gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none"
            >
                <span class="font-medium text-lg">
                    Should I ship PacketEvents with my project?
                </span>
                <svg
                    class="w-3 h-3 rotate-180 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-0 transition-transform"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                    fill="none"
                    viewBox="0 0 10 6"
                >
                    <path
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        stroke-linecap="round"
                        stroke-linejoin="round"
                        stroke-width="2"
                        d="M9 5 5 1 1 5"
                    ></path>
                </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="p-5 text-zinc-200">
                <p class="text-red-300">
                    It's best to avoid shipping PacketEvents with your project.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Ensuring your users only run a single instance of
                    PacketEvents will not only
                    <span class="text-indigo-300"> boost performance</span>,
                    but also <span class="text-indigo-300">streamline bug-reporting</span>.
                    Plus, you'll save time by not needing to update
                    with every new patch release.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>
    </div>
</div>
